  "favourites_count": 8,
  "description": "<h2>What it does</h2>\n<p>Vanilla behavior: applying a loadout preset strips <strong>all</strong> your equipment and re-equips from the preset. Slots the preset doesn’t define are left empty.</p>\n<p>With BetterLoadouts: only slots the preset defines are touched. Everything else stays equipped.</p>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p>You have a preset with just a weapon and armor. You’re wearing a helmet, headset, and backpack that aren’t in the preset.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Vanilla:</strong> helmet, headset, and backpack get unequipped. You have to re-equip them manually.</li>\n<li><strong>BetterLoadouts:</strong> weapon and armor swap in, helmet/headset/backpack stay on.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If the preset defines every slot, behavior is identical to vanilla.</p>\n",
